# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sheppard / IMU quantisation research project
#
# Rule of thumb: commit sources and documents, never build output, never
# vendor trees you did not write, never anything that can be regenerated by
# pressing a button.
#
# SECOND RULE, added for the release: nothing unpublished leaves this machine.
# The "Internal" block near the bottom is the one that enforces it. Read the
# note there before adding anything to the repository root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- STM32CubeIDE build output ---------------------------------------------
Debug/
Release/
*.o
*.d
*.su
*.map
*.list
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.srec

# CubeIDE / Eclipse workspace state. .project and .cproject ARE committed --
# without them the project will not import.
.settings/
.metadata/
*.launch
RemoteSystemsTempFiles/

# CubeMX scratch. The .ioc IS committed: it is the source of truth for the
# pin map and peripheral configuration.
.mxproject

# --- KiCad -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .history is KiCad's autosave/backup tree. It contains its own git repo with
# thousands of loose objects and must never be committed.
.history/
*-backups/
fp-info-cache
*.kicad_prl
*.bak
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.net
_autosave-*
*.lck

# Fabrication output is regenerated from the source files
production/
gerbers/
*.zip

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Data ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Campaign data belongs in Zenodo with a DOI, not in git.
Test Datasets/*
# The contents are excluded, not the directory: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so `Test Datasets/` followed by a
# negation silently does nothing.
*.csv
*.parquet
*.npy

# NO NEGATIONS HERE. Earlier revisions re-included summary.csv and the run
# plans. Both now stay out: the run plans are working documents that cite
# unpublished notes by number, and the summary is published through the data
# deposit instead, where it can carry a codebook and a licence.

# --- Deposit build output --------------------------------------------------
# zenodo/ holds the build script and the templates, which ARE tracked. The
# assembled tree and the bundles are output and regenerate on demand.
zenodo/build/
zenodo/*.zip

# --- Internal --------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT FOR RELEASE, ON GITHUB OR ANYWHERE ELSE, until the work is published.
#
# Everything matched below is either an unpublished finding, a working
# document that cites unpublished findings by number, or a record of how the
# project's own errors were found. None of it is needed to build the firmware,
# run the analysis or use the data deposit.
#
# NOTE: adding a pattern here stops future commits. It does NOT remove
# anything already in the repository's history. See zenodo/RELEASE.md.
TN-*.md
*_AUDIT_*.md
*_Audit_*.md
SUPERSEDED.md
SESSION_HANDOVER.md
DOCUMENTS_TO_ADD_TO_PROJECT.md
Table_Verification_*.md
Concept_Note*.md
Preprint_Scaffold*.md
ZENODO_DEPOSIT_PLAN.md
notes/
research/
corpus/
manuscript/
Misc/

# The manuscript and its supporting drafts.
paper/

# Documents in any format at the root, which is where drafts get dropped.
*.docx
*.pdf
!datasheets/**/*.pdf

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*~
*.swp

# --- Local tool state ------------------------------------------------------
.sheppard_console.json

# --- Generated figures ------------------------------------------------------
# All of them. The numbered result figures were tracked while the paper was
# built from this repository; they are build output of figures.py and they
# show unpublished results.
Figures/
